Threads UI (Right Sidebar) - Work Plan / Notes

Context
- Discord-like threads UI is implemented as a right sidebar (not inline below messages).
- Selecting text in a message + typing should start a new thread and seed the typed character.
- Selection also creates a persistent "comment-style" highlight; hover shows tooltip; click opens the thread.

User-reported issues to fix
1) Thread chat scroll/collapse
   - Scrolling in thread view doesn't reliably collapse the parent snippet card.
   - Collapsed header should be very compact (1 line feels best).
2) Selection -> type reliability
   - After repeated use, selection + typing sometimes stops opening the thread starter.
3) Thread starter composer UX
   - Starter composer must reuse the same input box component (not a plain TextArea).

Implementation plan
- Starter composer:
  - Replace the thread starter TextArea in `ThreadSidebar.tsx` with a small wrapper around `InputbarCore`.
  - Keep the send behavior custom: create thread via `createThreadFromMessageThunk(...)`, then navigate to thread chat.
  - Support "seed char" + buffered keystrokes via the existing EventEmitter flow.
- Selection reliability:
  - Extract a "computeSelectionContext()" function and call it both on selection events and on keydown (fallback).
  - Listen on `pointerup` in addition to `mouseup` + `selectionchange`.
  - Reset pending buffered-keystroke state when a new selection is detected.
- Thread chat collapse:
  - Collapse as soon as the user moves away from the bottom (`scrollTop > 0`).
  - Add a wheel fallback so collapse still happens even when scrollTop doesn't change (macOS rubberband / short threads).
  - Reduce collapsed header to a single line, tighter padding.

Validation checklist
- `pnpm lint`
- `pnpm test`
- `pnpm format`
